{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Landed as Gerrit change 1740 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1), merged to main as 432a92c165.\n\nreconcile-bridge.yml now fires on the single entry '23 * * * *' — off the top of the hour because :00 is GitHub's most contended and most frequently dropped scheduling slot. Worst-case Jira<->rebar sync latency is 1 hour, recorded in docs/jira-sync-setup.md. Jenkinsfile mirrors it; the canary is untouched at 2-hourly with its 4h window, which still clears the 3x-cadence floor now that the floor rises 2h -> 3h.\n\nThe cadence test still DERIVES fire times from the workflow's own cron rather than echoing a literal, and now also asserts exactly one schedule entry and a non-zero minute. Both were mutated locally to confirm they fail (a second entry -> gaps [30]; minute 0 -> the off-:00 assertion).\n\n*** OPERATOR ACTION REQUIRED — NOW ACTIONABLE ***\nThis change edits infra/terraform/monitoring_bridge.tf, and .github/workflows/terraform-drift.yml runs 'terraform plan -detailed-exitcode' on any infra/terraform/** change and FAILS on a non-empty plan. Terraform Drift will stay RED until someone runs terraform apply. Nothing in this repo can clear it; it needs AWS credentials this session does not hold.\n\nWhat the apply changes, so the diff is not a surprise: the bridge_run_failures alarm goes from threshold=1 / evaluation_periods=1 to threshold=0 / evaluation_periods=2 / datapoints_to_alarm=2. This was NOT cosmetic. The old tuning meant 'two failed passes inside one hour'; at an hourly cadence at most one pass lands in an hourly bucket, so the Sum could never exceed 1 and the alarm would have become structurally unfirable — silently, which is exactly the failure it was created to catch after the 2026-08-12 token expiry produced hours of outage with zero CloudWatch signal. Until the apply runs, the DEPLOYED alarm is still the old one, so bridge failures are currently unalarmed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786655598217093001,"uuid":"a9252c85-c6fc-45ce-b3fe-0d3aef65cebf"}